Passport runs games in software it does not include; install.sh downloads it:

- Voile, https://github.com/Zagrios/voile (latest runtime release, downloaded from there,
  including voile-lkd, FEX, DXMT, CrossOver's Wine and Valve's steamclient libraries, each under its own license, listed in the runtime's licenses folder).
- Valve's Linux steamclient, from Valve's Steam client update servers.

tool/launch.sh is Obelisk's launch.sh, https://github.com/Zagrios/Obelisk (GPL-3.0).

hook/ is forked from the dylib of NotProton, https://github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton (GPL-3.0), by NotProtonNot
and its contributors: the loader, signature resolver, hooks, web UI routes, patches to Steam's compatibility UI and the
signature databases in hook/signatures. The tool layout follows NotProton too.

hook/vendor/dobby is Dobby, https://github.com/jmpews/Dobby (Apache-2.0, license in that folder), unmodified at commit
5dfc8546954ce3b3198132ab13fddb89ee92cdd7 without its docs and tests. hook/build.sh builds it into the hook.

hook/vendor/cJSON.c and cJSON.h are cJSON (MIT), Copyright (c) 2009-2017 Dave Gamble and cJSON contributors. The
license is in the head of each file.
